'''''Olearia traversiorum''''', the '''Chatham Island akeake''', or '''Chatham Island tree daisy''', is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Asteraceae]]. It is [[endemic]] to the [[Chatham Islands]] of New Zealand. It is also known by the [[Synonym (taxonomy)|synonym]] ''O. traversii''.<ref name=nzpcn>
[https://www.nzpcn.org.nz/flora_details.asp?ID=609 Olearia traversiorum] on [[New Zealand Plant Conservation Network]] (NZPCN)</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.nzpcn.org.nz/flora/species/olearia-traversiorum/|title=Olearia traversiorum}}</ref>

== Taxonomy ==
{{Lang|la|traversiorum}} is an emendation of the originally described {{Lang|la|traversii}}, and is meant to honor both [[William Travers (New Zealand politician)|William Travers]] and his son [[Henry Travers (naturalist)|Henry Travers]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal |last1=Heenan |first1=P. B. |last2=de Lange |first2=P. J. |last3=Houliston |first3=G. J. |last4=Barnaud |first4=A. |last5=Murray |first5=B. G. |date=December 2008 |title=Olearia telmatica (Asteraceae: Astereae), a new tree species endemic to the Chatham Islands |url=http://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/00288250809509786 |journal=New Zealand Journal of Botany |language=en |volume=46 |issue=4 |pages=567–583 |doi=10.1080/00288250809509786 |bibcode=2008NZJB...46..567H |issn=0028-825X|url-access=subscription }}</ref>

== Human uses ==
''O. traversiorum'' is used both as a garden tree, and for firewood.<ref name=":0" /> It has also been exported, and can be grown in other areas with mild oceanic climates such as [[Scotland]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Gondwana |url=http://www.gcnursery.co.uk/gondwana.htm |publisher=Garden Cottage Nursery}}</ref>

